' purpose: offline TAR metadata inventory and mock-only completion boundary
' covers: tooling/native-ingress/tar-inventory.mjs
' covers: tooling/native-ingress/tar-inventory.test.mjs
' covers: tooling/native-ingress/inventory-controller.mjs
' covers: tooling/native-ingress/inventory-controller.test.mjs
' context: _spec/_plans/ml-runtime-redesign.md section 27 owns goals, scope and evidence.
' status: source mapped; canonical section 27 owns current synthetic verification and closing-review receipts.
' rendering: source keeps house include; approved local-theme substitution is renderer-input only.
@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
title Offline TAR inventory — streaming metadata, mock-only completion

actor "Trusted synthetic caller" as CALLER <<host>>
participant "inventory-controller.mjs\nrunMockInventory" as CONTROLLER <<app>>
participant "Mock source\nnext / return" as SOURCE <<async>>
participant "tar-inventory.mjs\ncreateTarInventory" as PARSER <<app>>
participant "Provisional metadata sink\ntrusted callback" as SINK <<host>>
participant "Node monotonic clock\nand cooperative timers" as CLOCK <<host>>
participant "InventoryError" as ERROR <<error>>

CALLER ARROW_MAIN CONTROLLER : runMockInventory(source, sink, tightened limits)
CONTROLLER ARROW_MAIN CLOCK : first START; total120s, work119s, cleanup reserve1s
CONTROLLER ARROW_MAIN CONTROLLER : capture strict own-data limits and mock protocol
CONTROLLER ARROW_MAIN PARSER : createTarInventory(tightened parser limits)
note over CONTROLLER, SOURCE
Mock markers assert a test protocol only.
Caller callbacks remain trusted code;
this module is not a capability sandbox.
No filesystem, network or child adapter.
end note

loop One pull at a time; no next pull until sink work finishes
  CONTROLLER ARROW_MAIN SOURCE : await next() within work deadline
  SOURCE ARROW_QUEUE CONTROLLER : bounded native byte chunk or mock completion
  alt Byte chunk
    CONTROLLER ARROW_MAIN PARSER : feed(bytes); admission before private copy
    PARSER ARROW_MAIN PARSER : parse headers / extensions / member bytes / padding
    note right of PARSER
512-byte basic / ustar / old-GNU headers
Checksum and bounded numeric fields
Octal digits must precede any NUL terminator
PAX local/global and GNU longname/link subset
Unknown keys, sparse layouts and kinds STOP
    end note
    PARSER ARROW_MAIN PARSER : canonical path collision checks; bounded metadata digest
    PARSER ARROW_MAIN CONTROLLER : frozen provisional events; no member contents
    loop Each provisional event
      CONTROLLER ARROW_MAIN SINK : await acceptance before next pull
    end
  else Source completes
    CONTROLLER ARROW_MAIN CONTROLLER : require explicit mock integrity and compressed-EOF flags
    CONTROLLER ARROW_MAIN CONTROLLER : accepted terminal receipt closes mock source contract
    CONTROLLER ARROW_MAIN PARSER : finish(): require complete framing and no pending member/extension
    PARSER ARROW_MAIN CONTROLLER : frozen TAR_INVENTORY summary
  end
end

note over PARSER, SINK
All expanded bytes and serialized metadata count.
Only explicit path aliases apply.
Link targets are data and never followed.
Events stay provisional until all gates pass.
end note

alt All parser, mock completion and sink gates pass
  CONTROLLER ARROW_MAIN CALLER : frozen MOCK_INVENTORY summary; mockOnly:true
else Parse, source, sink, limit or deadline failure
  CONTROLLER ARROW_ERROR CONTROLLER : absorb failure; no more pulls, parsing, sink work or success
  CONTROLLER ARROW_MAIN CLOCK : cleanupEnd=min(total end, failure time+1s)
  opt Acquired source without accepted completion and budget remains
    CONTROLLER ARROW_ERROR SOURCE : captured return at most once; bounded wait
  end
  opt Cleanup fails, rejects or remains uncertain
    CONTROLLER ARROW_ERROR ERROR : cleanup error supersedes first failure with cause
  end
  CONTROLLER ARROW_ERROR CALLER : throw failure; ignore handled late promise results
end

note over CALLER, ERROR
realArchiveInspected / decoderQualified:false
extractionAuthorized / nativeQualified:false
provenanceVerified:false
pythonFreeSubsetVerified:false
installedUsability/rustReady/trainingReady:false
end note

legend bottom
  Additive createTarMemberInventory shares this state machine and exposes final regular-file spans.
  Span JSON<=4MiB; offsets count consumed physical bytes after GNU/PAX header processing.
  Base feed events, metadata digests and existing summary schema remain unchanged.
  Parser/controller source and tests are synthetic offline infrastructure, not an XZ decoder.
  No archive read/stat/list, extraction, process, tool discovery or network belongs in this unit.
  Expanded<=1GiB; physical headers<=65536; total extension payload<=64KiB.
  Paths/links<=1024 bytes; chunks<=1MiB; data events<=32768.
  Event<=32768 bytes; total metadata<=16MiB; retained collision keys<=32MiB.
  Limits constrain source-accounted work, not native heap, callbacks or hard CPU/time containment.
  Mock next results are own-data done/value records; success receipts contain exactly three true flags.
  Valid mock completion closes its source contract even when later TAR finalization fails.
  Metadata SHA-256 binds ordered UTF-8 JSON events + LF, not discarded payload bytes.
  Real XZ framing/integrity, decoder qualification, SDK NoPython and Rust verification remain separate.
endlegend
@enduml
